@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Delete Account & Data";
    var today = DateTimeExtensions.PakistanToday().ToString("MMMM d, yyyy");
}
<div style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px 80px;font-family:-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif;color:#0f2220;line-height:1.65">
    <h1 style="font-size:28px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:4px">Delete Your Account &amp; Data</h1>
    <p style="color:#5c7a75;font-size:13.5px;margin-top:0">Last updated @today</p>

    <p>ScholarshipHive is an internal workforce attendance app — accounts are created and managed by an
    admin at your organization, and there's no self-service "delete my account" button in the app itself.
    That's deliberate: attendance and shift-report records are part of the company's own employment
    recordkeeping, and only an admin at your organization can authorize removing them.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">How to request deletion</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Ask your organization's ScholarshipHive admin directly (in person, or however you'd normally
            reach them), <b>or</b> email <a href="mailto:gmghulamgmghulam@gmail.com">gmghulamgmghulam@gmail.com</a> and
            we'll route the request to your organization's admin.</li>
        <li>Once confirmed, an admin deactivates and removes your account.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">What gets deleted</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Deleted:</b> your login credentials, device recognition data, and push-notification token.</li>
        <li><b>Retained</b> (as part of standard employment recordkeeping, per your organization's own
            retention policy): historical attendance records and submitted shift reports tied to your
            account while you were an active employee. These stay associated with your account internally
            but are no longer accessible to you once the account is removed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">Questions</h2>
    <p>See our <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for the full detail on what
    we collect and why, or email <a href="mailto:gmghulamgmghulam@gmail.com">gmghulamgmghulam@gmail.com</a> with any
    questions about this process.</p>
</div>
